{
  "context": "Post-process generated TBL/CSV files rather than modifying dbgen output.\nUse PyArrow's write_table() with sort_columns for Parquet output. New module\nbenchbox/core/data_organization/ should be called by the existing generator\npipeline after TBL generation, not replace it. Execute in three phases within\nthis TODO: (1) Parquet sorted export + CLI/config wiring, (2) clustering and\npartition-aware strategies, (3) Delta Lake and Iceberg integrations using the\nsame validated ordering abstractions and tests.\n",
  "description": "Enable BenchBox to generate benchmark datasets (TPC-H, TPC-DS, etc.) that are\npre-sorted or pre-clustered in open table formats like Parquet, Delta Lake,\nand Iceberg. This allows users to:\n\n1. Test zone map / data skipping effectiveness across platforms\n2. Compare sorted vs unsorted query performance\n3. Evaluate Z-order and Hilbert clustering strategies\n4. Create reproducible benchmark datasets with controlled data organization\n\nCurrently, BenchBox generates data in TBL format and loads it into platforms.\nThe data order depends on the dbgen tool output and platform loading behavior.\nThis TODO adds explicit control over data organization in the generated files.\n\nKey use cases:\n- Generate Parquet files sorted by date columns for time-series benchmarks\n- Create Z-ordered Delta Lake tables for multi-dimensional filtering\n- Produce Iceberg tables with optimized partition/sort strategies\n- Enable A/B testing of data organization strategies",
